TITLE:: SampleEditorDirtHost
summary:: the sample editor inside a SuperDirt: previews through orbits, reads saves back into the library's Buffers, loads banks
categories:: Libraries>SampleEditor
related:: Classes/SampleEditorHost, Classes/SampleEditor, Classes/SuperDirt

DESCRIPTION::
A link::Classes/SampleEditorHost:: that knows a SuperDirt. The menu beside play
lists its orbits, numbered from 0 as code::# orbit:: is, and the preview plays
at the head of the orbit's group into its dry bus, so that orbit's effects
apply; its always-on effects are woken first, since they pause after four
seconds of silence and only a set resumes them. A file the library holds opens
as code::bd:3:: and plays from the library's own Buffer, read first if the
library was made with code::doNotReadYet::.

A save reads the new file back into the same Buffer, the header first, so every
event keeps its bufnum and Tidal plays the new file at once under the same name
and number. A file saved into a bank's folder is appended to the bank. A bank
folder written by to bank... or export slices... is loaded, its new files only,
as the bank named after the folder.

code::
h = SampleEditorDirtHost(~dirt);
SampleEditor.defaultHost = h;
SampleEditor.sample(\bd, 3);             // bd:3 of the library
SampleEditor("~/x.wav");                 // any file; as bd:3 if the library holds it
::

Only SuperDirt's public methods are used and SuperDirt is never named, so the
class compiles without it.

An strong::owner:: does some of this itself: whatever of code::wakeOrbit::,
code::reloadSample::, code::addSample::, code::loadSamples::,
code::sampleAtPath:: and code::tags:: it answers is asked of it instead.
SuperDirtGUI makes its host this way (code::~sdg.editorHost::), so its window
hears of new banks and the editor reads and writes its tags.

